# NOTE (2026-07-13): the old per-section `/x/:slug -> /x/:slug/` rules are
# GONE deliberately. They also matched URLs that already had the trailing
# slash — real pages were shadowed by their files, but every UNKNOWN slug
# 301'd to itself in an infinite loop instead of reaching the 404 catch-all.
# Netlify normalizes no-slash -> slash for existing directories natively,
# so the dynamic rules were pure downside. Do not reintroduce them.

# --- VERA: public Little Fight product. The complete browser surface lives at
# /vera/ on this site. Its three sanitized data contracts are produced by the
# VERA engine's nightly cloud workflow and exposed through first-party URLs.
# 200! prevents an old built snapshot from shadowing the live feed.
/VERA             /vera/                                                          301
# Only the sanitized public lens is proxied. Private/raw hunt data never enters
# this repository, this Netlify property, or a browser response.
/vera/data/public.json https://raw.githubusercontent.com/omgitsthedm/vera-apartment-search/feed/public.json 200!
/vera/data/archive.json https://raw.githubusercontent.com/omgitsthedm/vera-apartment-search/feed/archive.json 200!
/vera/data/meta.json https://raw.githubusercontent.com/omgitsthedm/vera-apartment-search/feed/meta.json 200!

